From 86e36223e2a0de82615a9f5e2cd64ac867245f16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Pivoto <>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:27:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] fix(e2): keep SF readback within FlexRIC RIC and xApp
 buffers

The pinned near-RT RIC renders every SLICE indication into a 2048-byte stack
buffer without bounds (to_string_slice, influx listener), so the 13-label
readback crashed it with SIGSEGV. Pack the readback by priority (one
outcome, rules, up to 4 UEs, counters) under a budget computed with the
RIC's own formulas, and keep the xApp SQLite rows under its 4096-byte
buffer. Outcomes are now delivered FIFO, one per indication, on every tick
while any is unreported. A regression test renders the worst case with
FlexRIC's real to_string_slice() under ASan.
